{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition","id":701015,"title":"Resources as a Condition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-14T09:43:23-07:00","id":701015,"title":"Resources as a Condition","content":"While trying to figure out exactly how the Resources Merit and the Cash equipment interacted, I was struck by how similar Cash is to a Condition, so I whipped up a couple quick changes that I'll probably be using in future games. Hopefully, some of you will find this useful or interesting!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Resources (Merit *-*****)<br /> Effect: </b>At the beginning of each Chapter, the character takes the Cash Condition with rating equal to her Resources dots if she didn't already have it with an equal or greater rating.<br /> <i>At any time</i> a character may reduce their effective Resources by 1 for a month to take the Cash Condition with rating equal to their Resources plus 1. <i>This replaces a Cash Condition granted by the Merit if the character already had one.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cash Condition</b><br /> Money is burning a hole in your pocket, begging to be spent. This Condition is rated between 1 and 5.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When you flash your cash, you gain a bonus equal to its rating minus 2 to appropriate social actions. Additionally, you can buy as many items with Availability at least 2 lower than this Condition's rating as you want.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You may resolve this Condition to spend the money, which can provide a bonus to a single social action equal to the Condition's rating or buy an item with Availability equal or less than the rating. Alternately, you can shuffle your cash into your Resources, providing the Resource Merit with dots equal to the Condition's rating minus 1 for a month.<br /> <i>For example, a character with Cash 4 can buy as many Availability 1 or 2 items as they want, but must Resolve the Condition to buy an item with Availability 3 or 4.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The Wording would look so much nicer if WoD used variables like MtG, lol.<br /> <br /> I think this does a good job of bringing Resources forward, and showing inexperienced players what money can do in the system. Only two real differences from the existing system:<br /> <br /> First, spending your Cash gives you a Beat. Probably the biggest change, and I don't dislike it. It's easy enough to say that the Cash Condition doesn't grant Beats.<br /> <br /> I also reduced the Resources you can get from Cash, because just by the numbers you can get up to Resources 5 from Resources 1 by buying Cash then using it as Resources. This evens it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":".  Clarified that you can reduce your Resources at any time. 10-15-2015, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T09:54:14-07:00","id":701035,"title":"","content":"Well, It's not a bad hack, I'd say. It would probably make using Resources feel a bit more narratively relevant. I think I might use it. The issue, of course, is what happens if you raise Resources during a chapter.<br /> <br /> The neat part about using the Cash Condition, I think, is that it would provide a clear mechanical effect for a sudden, one-time influx of dosh. So, if you just pulled an Italian Job or won the lottery, you would have the Condition, but not have to spend Expriences on actual Resources dots.<br /> <br /> One change I would make is to make the Condition &quot;stacked&quot; instead of giving it a rating. It works basically the same, but I feel it would make the Condition a little easier to visualize, effectively &quot;spending&quot; one of the Cash conditions to get stuff, more like how money works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T10:03:51-07:00","id":701040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701035#post701035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, It's not a bad hack, I'd say. It would probably make using Resources feel a bit more narratively relevant. I think I might use it. The issue, of course, is what happens if you raise Resources during a chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, players usually spend Experiences between Chapters rather than during, but I'd probably rule as written: they don't gain the new Cash Condition until the beginning of the next Chapter. It'd probably be fine to give them the new Condition immediately if you don't mind players spending their cash twice, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701035#post701035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One change I would make is to make the Condition &quot;stacked&quot; instead of giving it a rating. It works basically the same, but I feel it would make the Condition a little easier to visualize, effectively &quot;spending&quot; one of the Cash conditions to get stuff, more like how money works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like &quot;At the beginning of each Chapter, gain levels of the Cash Condition up to your dots,&quot; and make resolving the Condition just remove a level of it? It's certainly easier to use but takes it a little further away from the current system (and allows players to get a little more mileage from their cash).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T14:26:13-07:00","id":701293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition#post701015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Effect: [/B]At the beginning of each Chapter, the character takes the Cash Condition with rating equal to her Resources dots if she didn't already have it with an equal or greater rating. A character may reduce their effective Resources by 1 for a month to take the Cash Condition with rating equal to their Resources plus 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest direct issue with this, compared to the RAW, is that it puts your major purchase as something you need to predict at the start of a Chapter. Instead of waiting to see what the Chapter might demand, If you have Resources 3, and you find yourself needing to make a Resources 4 purchase, your only options are to have predicted this ahead of time, or wait for the next Chapter. With the RAW you can wait to see what you might want to buy and if you want to take the reduction, you can do so when it comes up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Resolution:</b> You may resolve this Condition to spend the money, which can provide a bonus to a single social action equal to the Condition's rating or buy an item with Availability equal or less than the rating. Alternately, you can shuffle your cash into your Resources, providing the Resource Merit with dots equal to the Condition's rating minus 1 for a month.<br /> <i>For example, a character with Cash 4 can buy as many Availability 1 or 2 items as they want, but must Resolve the Condition to buy an item with Availability 3 or 4.</i> </div> </div> </div>What happens if you don't resolve the Condition? Do you keep racking them up? Or do they disappear?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this does a good job of bringing Resources forward, and showing inexperienced players what money can do in the system. Only two real differences from the existing system: </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it does that... all it does is make Cash a Condition instead of Equipment. It actually forces an extra step for players to learn (Resources &gt; Cash &gt; stuff, instead of just Resources &gt; stuff). I've never seen a player have trouble with what money can do in the 2e system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, spending your Cash gives you a Beat. Probably the biggest change, and I don't dislike it. It's easy enough to say that the Cash Condition doesn't grant Beats. </div> </div> </div>I really dislike this, and the idea of having to have a special Condition exception instead of just keeping Cash as a Equipment. Why on Earth should spending money get you XP?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also reduced the Resources you can get from Cash, because just by the numbers you can get up to Resources 5 from Resources 1 by buying Cash then using it as Resources. This evens it out. </div> </div> </div>Huh? This doesn't make any sense. Resources 1 lets you get 1 dot Cash equipment. There's no actual conversion rate, but even if you let them stack, it would take five purchases for 1 dot Cash to get a single Availability 5 purchase, while a Resources 5 character could have made five of them in the same amount of time. And the Resources 5 character gets all the Availability 1-3 stuff they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701035#post701035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The neat part about using the Cash Condition, I think, is that it would provide a clear mechanical effect for a sudden, one-time influx of dosh. So, if you just pulled an Italian Job or won the lottery, you would have the Condition, but not have to spend Expriences on actual Resources dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the RAW already has in the Cash and Contraband equipment stats. If get a major windfall, you get it in Cash or Contraband, which goes away after you spend it. You don't have to buy Resources because you robbed a bank to benefit from it mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T06:57:05-07:00","id":702038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701293#post701293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest direct issue with this, compared to the RAW, is that it puts your major purchase as something you need to predict at the start of a Chapter. Instead of waiting to see what the Chapter might demand, If you have Resources 3, and you find yourself needing to make a Resources 4 purchase, your only options are to have predicted this ahead of time, or wait for the next Chapter. With the RAW you can wait to see what you might want to buy and if you want to take the reduction, you can do so when it comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarified that you can reduce your Resources to make a big purchase at any time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701293#post701293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you don't resolve the Condition? Do you keep racking them up? Or do they disappear?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...if she didn't already have it with an equal or greater rating.&quot; - If you already have more Cash, you don't get any from Resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701293#post701293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it does that... all it does is make Cash a Condition instead of Equipment. It actually forces an extra step for players to learn (Resources &gt; Cash &gt; stuff, instead of just Resources &gt; stuff). I've never seen a player have trouble with what money can do in the 2e system.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players tend to write &quot;Resources ***&quot; or whatever on their sheet then forget about it, and they certainly don't know the specifics of how it allows them to acquire items and interacts with Availability until I explain it. They're mostly used to less abstract systems where you have a specific amount of money and each item has a distinct price. If your players are already comfortable and competent with the status quo, then I can see why it seems unnecessary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701293#post701293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike this, and the idea of having to have a special Condition exception instead of just keeping Cash as a Equipment. Why on Earth should spending money get you XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm OK with rewarding my players for using their resources, so although it wasn't my intention setting out to give Beats for spending money, I decided not to specify that it doesn't grant Beats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=701293#post701293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? This doesn't make any sense. Resources 1 lets you get 1 dot Cash equipment. There's no actual conversion rate, but even if you let them stack, it would take five purchases for 1 dot Cash to get a single Availability 5 purchase, while a Resources 5 character could have made five of them in the same amount of time. And the Resources 5 character gets all the Availability 1-3 stuff they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can reduce your Resources to get higher Availability items. Resources 1 -&gt; Resources 0, Cash 2. You can use Cash to get higher Resources for a month. Cash 2 -&gt; Resources 2. Repeat. The relevant sentence is on GMC 241 &quot;For more complex uses, consider it a single month's allotment of the same Resources.&quot; It's obviously a bug that no ST would actually let their player exploit, but I don't see any real reason not to patch it in my house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T10:04:31-07:00","id":702284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=702038#post702038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can reduce your Resources to get higher Availability items. Resources 1 -&gt; Resources 0, Cash 2. You can use Cash to get higher Resources for a month. Cash 2 -&gt; Resources 2. Repeat. The relevant sentence is on GMC 241 &amp;quot;For more complex uses, consider it a single month's allotment of the same Resources.&amp;quot; It's obviously a bug that no ST would actually let their player exploit, but I don't see any real reason not to patch it in my house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's entertain this idea for a moment. What if a player actually did this? What would that look like in the narrative? Using money to buy more money... sounds like a loan to me. Might want to slap an &quot;In Debt&quot; Condition on a player who did that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T13:39:24-07:00","id":702484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=702038#post702038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;...if she didn't already have it with an equal or greater rating.&quot; - If you already have more Cash, you don't get any from Resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>But nothing stops you from having Cash 1, Cash 2, Cash 3, etc. if you start low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My players tend to write &quot;Resources ***&quot; or whatever on their sheet then forget about it, and they certainly don't know the specifics of how it allows them to acquire items and interacts with Availability until I explain it. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can fix, &quot;My players don't read the rules,&quot; with more rules. Why are they going to pay more attention to Cash as a Condition that Resources generates, instead of equipment Resources generates? Especially since the actual impact is nearly identical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm OK with rewarding my players for using their resources, so although it wasn't my intention setting out to give Beats for spending money, I decided not to specify that it doesn't grant Beats. </div> </div> </div>Why does Resources get to be special though? You don't get beats for bringing your Allies, Contacts, Mentor, Retainers, etc. into play automatically via them generating Conditions to resolve. Having Resources stand out as a beat generator while the others don't do that sends a pretty weird signal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can reduce your Resources to get higher Availability items. Resources 1 -&gt; Resources 0, Cash 2. You can use Cash to get higher Resources for a month. Cash 2 -&gt; Resources 2. Repeat. The relevant sentence is on GMC 241 &quot;For more complex uses, consider it a single month's allotment of the same Resources.&quot; It's obviously a bug that no ST would actually let their player exploit, but I don't see any real reason not to patch it in my house rules. </div> </div> </div>This doesn't seem like a bug. This seems like a purposeful semantic run around of what the rules say.<br /> <br /> Having Cash 2 isn't the same as having Resources 2 for a month. That passage is clearly for &quot;more complex&quot; uses that don't interact with either Cash as equipment providing a dice bonus, or Cash providing single use Availability purchases. That line is for things like, &quot;cashing in a bunch of savings to live large for a month&quot; without trying to bookkeep how much renting nice clothes, going to nicer restaurants, etc. is going to break down in Availability.<br /> <br /> Using that clause in the Cash equipment and Resources 1 to get Cash 2, and using it to buy one Availability 2 item a Chapter for a month is not a bug; it is a clear misapplication of the rules since the second you make an Availability 1 or 2 purchase with your Cash, it goes away. The Cash equipment's &quot;more complex&quot; application is if you don't use Cash to buy something, or get a bonus to a roll with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T08:11:15-07:00","id":703477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=702284#post702284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's entertain this idea for a moment. What if a player actually did this? What would that look like in the narrative? Using money to buy more money... sounds like a loan to me. Might want to slap an &quot;In Debt&quot; Condition on a player who did that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would be a good response if a player actually tried this. &quot;Look, you can't make money appear out of thin air, but you can go get a loan. Do you want to get a loan?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=702484#post702484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But nothing stops you from having Cash 1, Cash 2, Cash 3, etc. if you start low.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Because on one hand, I don't think you should get more cash from Resources if you haven't spent last chapter's (because Resources specifies 1/chapter). But on the other hand, there should be some point to getting smaller amounts of cash in play.<br /> <br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n702484I don't think you can fix, &quot;My players don't read the rules,&quot; with more rules. Why are they going to pay more attention to Cash as a Condition that Resources generates, instead of equipment Resources generates? Especially since the actual impact is nearly identical.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> You could probably get the same effect by specifically giving the players the Cash equipment at the beginning of each chapter, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=702484#post702484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does Resources get to be special though? You don't get beats for bringing your Allies, Contacts, Mentor, Retainers, etc. into play automatically via them generating Conditions to resolve. Having Resources stand out as a beat generator while the others don't do that sends a pretty weird signal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'm not proposing a total reformation of the Merit system. I was just looking at how Resources and Cash worked, and was struck by some of the similarity to how Conditions work. So yes, this idea would make Resources stand apart from other social Merits. That is because it is an idea about the Resource Merit and not social Merits in general. If you don't like the Beats, it's easy enough to say it doesn't grant Beats. If you <i>also</i> don't like a Condition specifying that it doesn't grant Beats, it's easy enough to just stick with Cash equipment and not use this idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=702484#post702484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't seem like a bug. This seems like a purposeful semantic run around of what the rules say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're wrong! But I like making it sync up (Resources X -&gt; Cash X+1 / Cash X -&gt; Resources X-1). I don't think doing so causes any system problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T09:17:25-07:00","id":703559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=703477#post703477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably get the same effect by specifically giving the players the Cash equipment at the beginning of each chapter, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much skipping the point I'm making entirely. You've stated that a major motivation for house ruling this is because your players seem to neglect Resources, and especially its mechanical function in the game. You want your idea to bring Resources forward. I'm not seeing how it does that. It makes engaging in Resources more complicated (all Resources has to go through Cash first, rather than directly comparing Resources to Availability), which makes players less likely to engage with it. It bribes them a bit with a Beat, but given the restrictions on Beats from Condition resolutions, there are far simpler methods to getting that Beat; and Beat generation isn't even an intended consequence.<br /> <br /> The point isn't inherently the label slapped on Cash mechanically. The issue is the logic that adding a step will make players want to engage with something they aren't engaging with already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because I'm not proposing a total reformation of the Merit system. </div> </div> </div>House rules, in application, don't exist in a vacuum. Using your modification to Resources in an otherwise RAW game is going to be weird. That means there's a problem with this as a stand alone house rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...it's easy enough to just stick with Cash equipment and not use this idea. </div> </div> </div>Which I clearly will be doing.<br /> <br /> However that doesn't mean I can't look at your ideas and offer what I feel is useful criticism of them. Getting defensive and/or dismissive of dissent doesn't help you have the best house rule (whether I would use it or not).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think you're wrong! But I like making it sync up (Resources X -&gt; Cash X+1 / Cash X -&gt; Resources X-1). I don't think doing so causes any system problems. </div> </div> </div>Actually the way you have it phrased, it's pretty problematic. Since it either: (1) lets you boost your Resources monthly to absurdity or (2) lets you have exponentially growing number of instances of Resources.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alternately, you can shuffle your cash into your Resources, providing the Resource Merit with dots equal to the Condition's rating minus 1 for a month.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you take the first interpretation: Resources 3, becomes Resources 2/Cash 4, and then Cash 4 give me 3 more Resources dots, bringing me to Resources 5 for a month. As soon as I've done this, I reduce Resources again, it turns into Resources 5 -&gt; Resources 4/Cash 5 -&gt; Resources 8 for a month, etc. I continue to do this since it skips the per chapter basis, and I get to the point where I can effectively never run out of access to Cash, because I can grow my extra Resource Dots faster than they get reduced.<br /> <br /> If you take the second interpretation: Resources 3, becomes Resources 2/Cash 4, and then Cash 4 gets me a second Resources 3. I use the second Resources 3 to repeat, and I know how as many instances of Resources 2 as I want, and one Resources 3 at the end.<br /> <br /> Since we agree that reshuffling it into Resources was never the intent, why codify it? There's no way to make it good, just neutral (it is either bad, or there's no point in doing it). Either cut the idea completely, or clarify the intent we both agree the Cash Equipment write up communicates.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T05:00:12-07:00","id":960986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition?p=703559#post703559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Alternately, you can shuffle your cash into your Resources, providing the Resource Merit with dots equal to the Condition's rating minus 1 for a month.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you take the first interpretation: Resources 3, becomes Resources 2/Cash 4, and then Cash 4 give me 3 more Resources dots, bringing me to Resources 5 for a month. As soon as I've done this, I reduce Resources again, it turns into Resources 5 -&gt; Resources 4/Cash 5 -&gt; Resources 8 for a month, etc. I continue to do this since it skips the per chapter basis, and I get to the point where I can effectively never run out of access to Cash, because I can grow my extra Resource Dots faster than they get reduced.<br /> <br /> If you take the second interpretation: Resources 3, becomes Resources 2/Cash 4, and then Cash 4 gets me a second Resources 3. I use the second Resources 3 to repeat, and I know how as many instances of Resources 2 as I want, and one Resources 3 at the end.<br /> <br /> Since we agree that reshuffling it into Resources was never the intent, why codify it? There's no way to make it good, just neutral (it is either bad, or there's no point in doing it). Either cut the idea completely, or clarify the intent we both agree the Cash Equipment write up communicates.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the intention is that when you reshuffle you don't get your hand AND another hand on top of that.<br /> <br /> So, Resources 3 becomes Resources 2/Cash 4, and when you add Cash 4 to Resources 2 you get Resources 3 back. It's a reciprocal condition. R3 &lt;=&gt; R2+C4.<br /> <br /> Case 1: Your character gets Equipment: Cash 4. If you liquidize your Cash 4 Assets, you can have Resources 3 for one month, at the end of which you're back to having Resources 0.<br /> Case 2: Your character has Resources 3. Your Character decides to buy Equipment: Cash 4. Now your character has Resources 2 and Cash 4 until the end of the month.<br /> Case 3: Your character has Resources 2 and Cash 4. Your character decides to buy Resources 3 by combining Resources 2 + Cash 4, but it lasts for just one month, at the end of which it goes back to normal resources level (in this case Resources 2).<br /> <br /> The way the OP phrased it, when combining Cases 1 through 3 you get:<br /> <br /> Your character has Resources 3. The character buys Cash 4 and gets Resources 2. At the end of the month the character will be back to Resources 3. Should the character wish to buy Resources 3 it must recombine Cash 4 into the Resources 2, or wait a full-month.<br /> <br /> Also remember, Resources isn't linear in progression, it's closer to exponential. Resources 2 + Resources 2 will never give you Resources 4, it'll give you, at the most, Resources 3.<br /> Resources 0 is just barely enough for paying rent, bills, food and having $10 in your pocket.<br /> Resources 1 adds up to paid bills, rent, better food and about $50-150 at the end of the month. (price of a Kevlar vest rounding the $100)<br /> Resources 2 will raise that to about $170-250 (price range of a good enough rapier)<br /> Resources 3 to around $500-750;<br /> Resources 4 is about $1500 or more;<br /> Resources 5 could go for $5000/month spending money.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T08:37:11-07:00","id":961071,"title":"","content":"That's... a bit of a necro....<br /> <br /> Anyway, Resources don't work like that. There aren't monetary values attached to it, as it has been completely abstracted to interact with the Availability system instead of raw numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}